/// Granted licenses in License Manager in the License Manager User Guide .
/// Set the type of grant with the GrantType field: BuyerGrant - The default
/// grant type, created by the seller when a customer subscribes to a
/// product. The seller creates a license for the subscription and a buyer
/// grant for the customer. With a buyer grant, the customer can use,
/// consume, and distribute the license, according to the permissions the
/// seller sets in the product contract. DelegateGrant - A delegate grant
/// gives the grantee read-only visibility into the licenses and grants that
/// you have distributed to buyers for a product. The grantee can monitor
/// that activity on your behalf, and can also listen for the related Amazon
/// EventBridge events. A delegate grant conveys no entitlement to use the
/// licenses, and its only allowed operation is ListReceivedLicenses . You
/// must create the delegate grant, and its license, from the same Amazon
